{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100791","id":2251065539,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6GLIjD","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100791","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100791.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100791.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100791","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100791/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100791/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100791/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/ee48457828f1cc9bc679a3c372ed30a01935fd5f","number":100791,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[Input] Get mapped joy events for joypad","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Get the buttons and axes mapped to the connected joypad w/o having to use them all.\r\n\r\nMotivation behind this PR:\r\n* I want the user to be able to change their mappings in-game. This requires knowledge about the capabilities of their connected joypad. It also allows me to fetch a different joypad image.\r\n  * different joypads have different buttons/axes available: some joypads have `JOY_BUTTON_PADDLE_*`, some don't. Some don't have `JOY_BUTTON_MISC1`, or `JOY_AXIS_RIGHT_*`, etc.\r\n* Using the joypad name is not reliable, as the same joypad can have different names on different platforms/APIs.\r\n  * the guid is also not sensible\r\n\r\n\r\nSee attached test project:\r\n[joypad-event-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18240367/joypad-event-test.zip)\r\n\r\n\r\nOutput for my joypad using the test project:\r\n```\r\nXbox 360 Controller\r\n[\"a\", \"b\", \"x\", \"y\", \"back\", \"guide\", \"start\", \"leftstick\", \"rightstick\", \"leftshoulder\", \"rightshoulder\", \"dpup\", \"dpdown\", \"dpleft\", \"dpright\"]\r\n[\"leftx\", \"lefty\", \"rightx\", \"righty\", \"lefttrigger\", \"righttrigger\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\nfixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12564","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310664,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA2NjQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:input","name":"topic:input","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator